      "text": "To solve for \\( t \\), we start by using Viète's formulas for the roots of the polynomial \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0 \\), which are \\( a, b, \\) and \\( c \\). According to Viète's formulas, we have:\n\\[\na + b + c = -3,\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = 4,\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = 11.\n\\]\n\nNext, we consider the polynomial \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) whose roots are \\( a+b, b+c, \\) and \\( c+a \\). Using Viète's formulas again, we need to find the sums and products of these roots:\n\\[\n(a+b) + (b+c) + (c+a) = 2(a + b + c) = 2(-3) = -6,\n\\]\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) + (b+c)(c+a) + (c+a)(a+b) = \\sum_{\\text{cyc}} (ab + bc + ca) = 4 + 4 + 4 = 12,\n\\]\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = abc + ab(a+c) + bc(b+a) + ca(b+c) = 11 + a^2b + ab^2 + b^2c + bc^2 + c^2a + a^2c + ac^2 = 11 + ab(a+b+c) + bc(b+c+a) + ca(c+a+b) = 11 + 4 \\cdot (-3) + 4 \\cdot 11 = 11 - 12 + 44 = 43.\n\\]\nThus, the polynomial can be written as:\n\\[\nx^3 - (-6)x^2 + 12x - 43 = x^3 + 6x^2 + 12x - 43.\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\( t \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{43}.\n\\]",
