      "text": "Given the polynomial \\(x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0\\) with roots \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\), we use Vieta's formulas to find the relationships between the roots and the coefficients of the polynomial. According to Vieta's formulas, we have:\n\\[\na + b + c = -3,\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = 4,\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = 11.\n\\]\n\nThe polynomial \\(x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0\\) has roots \\(a+b\\), \\(b+c\\), and \\(c+a\\). To find the constant term \\(t\\), we need to determine the product of these roots, which is given by:\n\\[\n(ab + bc + ca) = 4,\n\\]\nindicating that the constant term \\(t\\) is:\n\\[\nt = -abc = -11.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(t\\) is \\(\\boxed{-11}\\).",
